1
00:00:00,863 --> 00:00:04,863
[bright music]

2
00:00:36,916 --> 00:00:38,749
Bestfriend,

3
00:00:38,791 --> 00:00:42,124
just the other day, you were on cloud nine.

4
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,999
But now, it seems like you're mourning.

5
00:00:45,041 --> 00:00:48,083
Try to understand him too.

6
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:51,958
He had his own life
before the two of you met.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,166
You can't suddenly
become everything in his life.

8
00:00:55,208 --> 00:00:56,708
Same with you.

9
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,854
Didn't it take you
quite a while to get over

10
00:00:58,896 --> 00:01:01,000
that long-distance relationship of yours?

11
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,750
The point is, he lied to me.

12
00:01:04,416 --> 00:01:08,416
He said he would donate
those clothes to a charity.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,666
That's why I was so clueless
when I spoke to his ex in the store.

14
00:01:13,708 --> 00:01:17,916
But you're just like him! You also lied to
your mom when you lost her money, remember?

15
00:01:17,958 --> 00:01:20,749
Because you love her.

16
00:01:20,791 --> 00:01:23,166
You didn't want her
to feel hurt or anxious.

17
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,999
It's just the same with K-pop!

18
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:27,291
He doesn't want you to
feel hurt or worried because...

19
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:29,583
I'm not sure about that, bestfriend.

20
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:31,791
Maybe it's better to avoid him for now.

21
00:01:32,416 --> 00:01:34,208
How will you do that?

22
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:36,916
You live under the same roof.

23
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:41,208
You eat from the same plate that he uses.

24
00:01:41,583 --> 00:01:45,041
You drink from the same glass he does.

25
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:48,125
- You poop in the same - - Eew!

26
00:01:48,416 --> 00:01:49,500
I get it.

27
00:01:50,583 --> 00:01:52,958
Why do you need to avoid him, anyway?

28
00:01:53,208 --> 00:01:56,791
Shouldn't you be there to support him?

29
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,708
Moving on from a past
relationship is not that easy.

30
00:02:02,166 --> 00:02:05,125
Think about it, you were in a long-distance
relationship for six months only.

31
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:08,833
But after the breakup,
you almost committed...

32
00:02:09,125 --> 00:02:11,958
Forget it. Let's not
talk about it, anymore.

33
00:02:13,125 --> 00:02:14,958
That's exactly my point!

34
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,583
It's not easy to move on from someone
you've been with for that many years.

35
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:21,833
What if he still cares about him?

36
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:24,750
What if he still loves him?

37
00:02:25,791 --> 00:02:27,791
What if I'm just a rebound?

38
00:02:27,958 --> 00:02:30,916
Finally! That's the reason behind it all!

39
00:02:30,958 --> 00:02:34,708
Why are you even comparing
yourself to K-pop's ex?

40
00:02:34,916 --> 00:02:39,250
That's not love! That's pride!

41
00:02:41,416 --> 00:02:47,166
Fine, but there's a big possibility
that he still feels something for him.

42
00:02:47,916 --> 00:02:51,291
Maybe he's just using
me to get back at him.

43
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:53,958
He already returned the clothes, right?

44
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,951
So it means you're not a rebound!

45
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:56,583
[soft music]

46
00:02:56,625 --> 00:02:59,833
Why does he get mad
each time I call him Josh?

47
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,958
Simple! He remembers his
ex every time you call him Josh.

48
00:03:04,166 --> 00:03:06,791
He wants to move on!

49
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,625
What are you going to do now, bestfriend?

50
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:15,083
How will you avoid him?

51
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:17,416
Where will you stay?

52
00:03:18,416 --> 00:03:20,000
I don't know.

53
00:03:20,583 --> 00:03:23,416
I'm thinking about taking
a few days off from work.

54
00:03:24,541 --> 00:03:27,708
I told you to take things slowly.

55
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:33,625
You love deeply, yet
you're also very insecure.

56
00:03:35,791 --> 00:03:37,958
Why not come home instead?

57
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:41,958
There’s no longer a
reason for you to stay there.

58
00:03:42,583 --> 00:03:46,583
You probably won't find that
disgusting scammer anymore.

59
00:03:48,305 --> 00:03:52,305
[soft music]

60
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:24,800
[soft music]

61
00:05:01,076 --> 00:05:05,076
[soft music]

62
00:05:55,083 --> 00:05:57,083
Hi, Mom, how are you?

63
00:05:57,583 --> 00:06:00,375
I'm doing okay, son. How about you?

64
00:06:00,541 --> 00:06:02,083
I'm okay, too.

65
00:06:03,375 --> 00:06:05,375
Looks like you're headed somewhere?

66
00:06:05,916 --> 00:06:09,416
I'm stepping outside for
a bit to get some fresh air.

67
00:06:09,458 --> 00:06:11,458
Alright, this won’t take up much time.

68
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,791
Your Aunt Susan called.

69
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:21,791
She needs to borrow money because your
cousin Junjun is still in the hospital.

70
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:27,083
I'm thinking of lending them some
because I feel bad for their situation.

71
00:06:27,125 --> 00:06:31,083
Your cousin has been in the
hospital for quite a while now.

72
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:33,333
Their hospital bill is piling up.

73
00:06:34,458 --> 00:06:35,958
Okay, Mom.

74
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,791
How much are we planning to send them?

75
00:06:39,375 --> 00:06:42,875
They're asking for 40,000 pesos.

76
00:06:44,666 --> 00:06:48,624
But I told them that we
don't have that kind of money.

77
00:06:48,666 --> 00:06:54,000
Maybe we can send them half?

78
00:06:55,625 --> 00:06:59,625
Okay, Mom, I'll send them
twenty thousand pesos.

79
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:04,375
But are you sure you'll have
enough money left for yourself?

80
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:06,291
Yes, Mom, don't worry.

81
00:07:06,333 --> 00:07:10,916
Just send me the full name,
address, and contact number.

82
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,833
Okay, I’ll send it to you.

83
00:07:13,875 --> 00:07:18,583
Thank you so much,
son. You're truly reliable.

84
00:07:20,416 --> 00:07:24,249
Okay, I won't hold you up any further.

85
00:07:24,291 --> 00:07:26,541
I’ll call you again, okay?

86
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:28,916
Love you, son. Thank you.

87
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:32,875
Love you too, Mom. Take care.

88
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:53,083
Where have you been?

89
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:55,666
I've been calling you. You
haven’t been picking up.

90
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,458
Oh, uh,

91
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,374
I was just with my girl friend.

92
00:08:03,416 --> 00:08:05,166
Or not my “girlfriend” girl friend.

93
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:06,458
Just uh,

94
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:09,291
a friend who happens to be a girl.

95
00:08:09,791 --> 00:08:11,291
What's her name?

96
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:13,499
Her name? Uh…

97
00:08:13,541 --> 00:08:15,291
Mitch… Mitchie...

98
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:16,708
Friend of mine from high school.

99
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:18,500
Where was she coming in from?

100
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:20,999
Well, uh... from San... Francisco.

101
00:08:21,041 --> 00:08:22,166
San Francisco!

102
00:08:23,208 --> 00:08:24,583
How did she get into LA?

103
00:08:24,625 --> 00:08:26,500
Well, she... she drove.

104
00:08:26,916 --> 00:08:28,083
Wow.

105
00:08:28,416 --> 00:08:30,541
You must be very special to her.

106
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,416
What? Why?

107
00:08:32,458 --> 00:08:34,291
To make time for you like that.

108
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:37,208
San Francisco to LA is
like a six, seven hour-drive.

109
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,708
She must’ve been real tired.

110
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:40,458
Yeah, yeah... She was.

111
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,249
But she was only here for one night.

112
00:08:42,291 --> 00:08:44,333
And I have to leave soon so

113
00:08:44,458 --> 00:08:46,208
it just made sense.

114
00:08:48,708 --> 00:08:49,708
Oh,

115
00:08:50,291 --> 00:08:52,666
I got this for you, by the way.

116
00:08:53,708 --> 00:08:56,083
Thank you. Am I still
picking you up tonight.

117
00:08:56,583 --> 00:08:57,916
Oh, no need, uh...

118
00:08:58,416 --> 00:09:00,208
Michelle, or Mitchie,

119
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,541
she’s going to pick me up tonight.

120
00:09:05,291 --> 00:09:07,250
Didn’t you just see each other?

121
00:09:08,083 --> 00:09:10,958
Yeah, but you know, it was super brief.

122
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,833
Because like you mentioned,
um, 6 1/2, 7-hour long drive...

123
00:09:13,875 --> 00:09:15,916
That’s just… She was really tired.

124
00:09:15,958 --> 00:09:18,250
Right. I thought she was
just staying for one night?

125
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:19,541
Yeah, yeah, um...

126
00:09:19,583 --> 00:09:20,208
yeah, we're...

127
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:21,333
well, yeah, but...

128
00:09:21,375 --> 00:09:24,458
I mean it was such a long drive…

129
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,249
That we didn’t meet for a long time.

130
00:09:26,291 --> 00:09:27,916
So we just...

131
00:09:28,791 --> 00:09:31,041
we just thought we’re gonna do it again.

132
00:09:32,291 --> 00:09:33,125
Okay.

133
00:09:34,166 --> 00:09:36,291
Do you want me to come pick you up

134
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:39,874
and bring you to wherever it is you're
going after your meeting with your

135
00:09:39,916 --> 00:09:41,041
“friend”?

136
00:09:42,166 --> 00:09:42,958
No need. She's...

137
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,086
She’s got it.

138
00:09:44,128 --> 00:09:45,958
[soft music]

139
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,333
All right,

140
00:09:47,833 --> 00:09:49,375
I’ll see you at ten.

141
00:09:49,916 --> 00:09:50,375
Wait, no, no,

142
00:09:50,417 --> 00:09:54,333
but she’s gonna be the
one who actually drives me.

143
00:09:54,666 --> 00:09:58,000
Yeah, I have to come
back and lock up the store.

144
00:09:58,291 --> 00:09:59,791
Oh yeah, yeah. Right, right.

145
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:00,750
Okay.

146
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:21,826
[soft music]

147
00:11:29,635 --> 00:11:33,635
[soft music]

148
00:11:57,488 --> 00:12:01,488
[soft music]

149
00:12:42,725 --> 00:12:46,725
[soft music]

150
00:13:14,875 --> 00:13:17,041
Oh, shoot. You’re still here.

151
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,041
Hello?

152
00:13:25,333 --> 00:13:27,458
Where did you go?

153
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:31,820
[bright music]

154
00:13:34,166 --> 00:13:35,541
So,

155
00:13:36,083 --> 00:13:40,125
you're the one that my brother's
doing all this cooking for?

156
00:13:40,583 --> 00:13:43,000
I have to say I’m pretty jealous.

157
00:13:43,208 --> 00:13:45,166
My brother would never do that for me.

158
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:48,625
How did you get inside?

159
00:13:49,166 --> 00:13:53,041
I might know where my little
brother puts his spare keys.

160
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:57,833
[bright music]

161
00:13:58,708 --> 00:14:00,083
Do you…

162
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,083
do you smell that?

163
00:14:02,125 --> 00:14:03,166
What?

164
00:14:05,541 --> 00:14:06,291
What?

165
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:08,249
I don’t know. Something...

166
00:14:08,291 --> 00:14:09,875
bad, just...

167
00:14:10,041 --> 00:14:11,791
really stinky.

168
00:14:12,041 --> 00:14:13,487
I don’t know where
it’s coming from though.

169
00:14:13,529 --> 00:14:14,625
Yeah, I don’t know but, um,

170
00:14:14,791 --> 00:14:17,041
I’m gonna go take a quick
shower. I'll be right back.

171
00:14:21,166 --> 00:14:22,208
Nice meeting you.

172
00:14:28,416 --> 00:14:29,458
Awww...

173
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:33,375
My little brother is so inspired.

174
00:14:36,892 --> 00:14:40,892
[bright music]

175
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:48,041
Now I know why.

176
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:54,208
Don't worry about me.

177
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:57,416
My brother's happiness is everything.

178
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:59,875
Does he know you're here?

179
00:15:00,166 --> 00:15:01,208
No.

180
00:15:01,708 --> 00:15:05,291
- Oh, did you want me to call him?
- Please don't.

181
00:15:05,916 --> 00:15:08,291
But I thought you're here to visit him?

182
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:10,083
Yeah, I am.

183
00:15:10,416 --> 00:15:13,000
Of course, I want to see him.

184
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:17,791
The question is,

185
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,125
does he even want to see me?

186
00:15:22,375 --> 00:15:23,416
What?

187
00:15:23,458 --> 00:15:25,500
He didn't even tell you about me yet?

188
00:15:29,708 --> 00:15:31,875
My brother ran away from home.

189
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:33,541
Four years ago.

190
00:15:35,666 --> 00:15:36,583
Why?

191
00:15:38,916 --> 00:15:40,958
Our father, he’s...

192
00:15:41,791 --> 00:15:43,416
very very strict.

193
00:15:43,458 --> 00:15:44,375
Um,

194
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:47,583
and my brother being the only son,

195
00:15:47,625 --> 00:15:50,125
all the expectations were put on him.

196
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,333
And with him being gay, I mean,

197
00:15:53,375 --> 00:15:55,624
our whole family knew,

198
00:15:55,666 --> 00:15:57,416
even my dad,

199
00:15:57,458 --> 00:16:00,166
except he’s in complete denial.

200
00:16:00,791 --> 00:16:03,249
So even though it was this open secret,

201
00:16:03,291 --> 00:16:06,458
my brother still had
to come out officially,

202
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:10,791
so that he could live his
life how he wanted to and

203
00:16:11,041 --> 00:16:13,500
be with people he wanted to be.

204
00:16:14,916 --> 00:16:16,500
My dad

205
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:19,458
did not want to accept that and

206
00:16:19,916 --> 00:16:22,583
he tried to send my
brother to the military.

207
00:16:23,208 --> 00:16:26,000
I think he thought that it would

208
00:16:26,125 --> 00:16:30,750
transform Joshua into
his idea of a real man.

209
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:36,291
As if Joshua doing a thousand sit-ups
here and a thousand push-ups there

210
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:40,666
would make him just get up and
announce to everyone “I’m a real man now.”

211
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,250
I mean, obviously Joshua
wasn’t go through with it.

212
00:16:44,547 --> 00:16:45,083
[soft music]

213
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:46,375
But, um,

214
00:16:46,791 --> 00:16:51,249
it pushed him to ran away and

215
00:16:51,291 --> 00:16:53,750
just leave all of that behind.

216
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:58,666
I did stay in touch with him
though, at least in the beginning.

217
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:00,416
I...

218
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:05,166
I never got to see him but we
were e-mailing pretty regularly.

219
00:17:05,333 --> 00:17:08,874
I knew where he was
staying, where he was working,

220
00:17:08,916 --> 00:17:12,125
all of his schedules and things like that.

221
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,499
Um, yeah...

222
00:17:14,541 --> 00:17:18,958
It’s been about a year
since we’ve spoken though.

223
00:17:20,958 --> 00:17:23,416
Why did he just stop talking to you?

224
00:17:25,978 --> 00:17:29,624
[soft music]

225
00:17:29,666 --> 00:17:33,625
I broke a promise that I made with him.

226
00:17:35,458 --> 00:17:37,666
What promise was that?

227
00:17:39,583 --> 00:17:42,791
That I would never tell our parents

228
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:45,833
that we were in communication.

229
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:51,041
Why did you do that?

230
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:57,000
I didn’t really have a choice.

231
00:17:58,750 --> 00:18:03,458
When Joshua broke up with his
boyfriend, I had to tell our mom.

232
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,874
Has he ever told you about him?

233
00:18:05,916 --> 00:18:07,166
Ivan?

234
00:18:09,291 --> 00:18:10,250
Yeah.

235
00:18:10,541 --> 00:18:12,416
When Ivan first moved to the US,

236
00:18:12,458 --> 00:18:15,874
my brother was the one who
was helping him with everything

237
00:18:15,916 --> 00:18:18,791
in helping him get settled in here.

238
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:21,624
He was just so in love with him,

239
00:18:21,666 --> 00:18:23,583
absolutely head over heels.

240
00:18:25,125 --> 00:18:28,359
I think it was the first time in so many

241
00:18:28,401 --> 00:18:32,124
years that my brother
felt like somebody truly

242
00:18:32,166 --> 00:18:36,083
loved him and embraced him for who he was,

243
00:18:36,125 --> 00:18:38,333
no questions asked.

244
00:18:39,458 --> 00:18:42,208
And they were really happy together.

245
00:18:44,583 --> 00:18:48,041
But then everything
changed when Ivan got a job.

246
00:18:48,083 --> 00:18:52,250
You know, he got his papers,
started working at this hospital, and...

247
00:18:53,375 --> 00:18:56,416
he met this doctor
there, a super-rich doctor.

248
00:18:56,458 --> 00:18:57,791
I don’t know.

249
00:18:58,250 --> 00:19:02,000
And they had this secret
affair for more than a year.

250
00:19:05,041 --> 00:19:06,833
When Joshua found out,

251
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,333
it just broke him.

252
00:19:10,625 --> 00:19:13,166
He couldn’t deal with it, you know, so

253
00:19:13,458 --> 00:19:16,958
he broke up with Ivan and
moved out of their apartment. But...

254
00:19:17,625 --> 00:19:19,416
he had nowhere to go.

255
00:19:20,958 --> 00:19:22,791
I mean, he had no one else.

256
00:19:22,833 --> 00:19:23,999
He literally had nothing.

257
00:19:24,041 --> 00:19:27,541
I don’t think he could even afford
to buy an airbed or anything. And I -

258
00:19:30,625 --> 00:19:33,124
I was just afraid that he would starve

259
00:19:33,166 --> 00:19:36,416
or I’ll get a call that he was
dead on the street somewhere.

260
00:19:36,458 --> 00:19:39,375
I... I didn’t know what else to do, so

261
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:43,875
I had to break our
promise and I told my mom.

262
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:49,541
So she gave me some
money to send to Joshua.

263
00:19:50,008 --> 00:19:51,666
[soft music]

264
00:19:51,708 --> 00:19:53,666
He didn’t accept the money, though.

265
00:19:54,083 --> 00:19:56,500
He thought it was from our father.

266
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:58,625
He said

267
00:20:00,041 --> 00:20:01,624
he'd rather die

268
00:20:01,666 --> 00:20:07,833
than to ask for help from somebody
who couldn’t accept him for who he was.

269
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:12,875
He sent back all the money and…

270
00:20:13,166 --> 00:20:16,666
I haven’t been able to
reach him ever since.

271
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:22,541
How did you even know where he
lives now? How did you find him?

272
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:26,625
Okay, please don't tell him.

273
00:20:26,916 --> 00:20:29,750
And I’m not proud of what I did but

274
00:20:29,958 --> 00:20:33,458
I might have figured
out his e-mail password.

275
00:20:34,750 --> 00:20:37,708
It's his birthday, if you
can even believe that!

276
00:20:37,750 --> 00:20:41,833
He has this big ego and
pride and whatnot but

277
00:20:41,875 --> 00:20:45,083
his email password is just his birthday!

278
00:20:46,875 --> 00:20:49,749
I just couldn’t keep watching my mom

279
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:53,625
wither away being so
worried sick about him and…

280
00:20:54,946 --> 00:20:56,249
[soft music]

281
00:20:56,291 --> 00:20:58,125
our dad too.

282
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:01,583
He’ll never admit that but…

283
00:21:02,541 --> 00:21:05,708
he asks about Joshua almost everyday.

284
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:18,833
But now I am just...

285
00:21:19,625 --> 00:21:21,708
I'm so relieved.

286
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:25,541
My brother is cooking for someone again.

287
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:32,208
I just want you to be happy and maybe

288
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:35,333
Joshua will call me one day and say

289
00:21:35,416 --> 00:21:37,833
guess what I cooked for, um...

290
00:21:40,583 --> 00:21:42,833
what… what is your name?

291
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,333
Andre?

292
00:21:44,750 --> 00:21:46,333
Are you asking me?

293
00:21:47,125 --> 00:21:48,250
It’s Andre.

294
00:21:50,375 --> 00:21:51,375
Andre.

295
00:21:52,875 --> 00:21:54,208
Just, um...

296
00:21:55,250 --> 00:21:58,833
try to be patient with my little brother.

297
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:02,958
He can be very sensitive,

298
00:22:03,958 --> 00:22:06,625
Given everything he's been through.

299
00:22:22,885 --> 00:22:26,885
[soft music]

300
00:22:37,208 --> 00:22:39,958
- Here's your change. Have a good day.
- Thanks. You too.

301
00:22:44,375 --> 00:22:47,583
You're early. Did you have
a good time with your friend?

302
00:22:59,083 --> 00:23:01,125
Okay, get off. What if a customer sees?

303
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:02,416
I don't care.

304
00:23:06,833 --> 00:23:08,875
You slept with your friend, didn't you?

305
00:23:09,541 --> 00:23:10,541
What?

306
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:11,916
No!

307
00:23:12,208 --> 00:23:13,291
Just be honest.

308
00:23:13,333 --> 00:23:15,208
I won’t be pissed if your honest.

309
00:23:16,125 --> 00:23:17,583
I didn't sleep with anyone.

310
00:23:18,375 --> 00:23:20,083
Then why are you being so sweet?

311
00:23:20,958 --> 00:23:22,625
Am I not allowed to be sweet?

312
00:23:23,875 --> 00:23:26,000
I hate men.

313
00:23:26,458 --> 00:23:28,291
You just cheat

314
00:23:28,458 --> 00:23:32,208
and then act extra sweet to cover it up.

315
00:23:35,083 --> 00:23:37,708
Joshua, I didn’t cheat on you.

316
00:23:39,375 --> 00:23:41,833
After spending the whole
night with your friend?

317
00:23:41,875 --> 00:23:42,666
Come on!

318
00:23:42,708 --> 00:23:44,958
My friend Michelle.

319
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,541
What if it it’s not Michelle?

320
00:23:46,708 --> 00:23:48,250
What if it's a Michael?

321
00:23:52,416 --> 00:23:53,583
Okay, there's no Michelle,

322
00:23:53,625 --> 00:23:54,875
there’s no Michael,

323
00:23:55,625 --> 00:23:57,750
there's no cheating, that’s for sure.

324
00:23:58,791 --> 00:23:59,708
I lied.

325
00:24:00,416 --> 00:24:02,291
But I only did it because...

326
00:24:03,791 --> 00:24:04,750
I was jealous.

327
00:24:07,125 --> 00:24:08,833
Why would you be jealous?

328
00:24:33,291 --> 00:24:37,000
I’m sorry. I didn't tell you sooner.

329
00:24:37,222 --> 00:24:39,499
[dramatic music]

330
00:24:39,541 --> 00:24:41,083
I... I just

331
00:24:42,375 --> 00:24:45,375
I didn’t want you to think that I -

332
00:24:47,833 --> 00:24:48,666
It’s okay.

333
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:51,833
It doesn’t even matter.

334
00:25:13,897 --> 00:25:17,897
[dramatic music]

335
00:25:44,258 --> 00:25:48,258
[dramatic music]

336
00:26:41,275 --> 00:26:45,275
[dramatic music]
